  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Experimental Affinities in Music (2015), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 3 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Experimental Affinities in Music by Paulo De Assis was published by Leuven University Press in 2015. Conceptually, the work connects to Affinities, Biology and Biochemistry.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 3 citations. Citations peaked in 2019 with 1 citing works. Notable citing venues include Eighteenth Century Music. The citing works include 1 journal article, 1 book chapter and 1 dissertation. The citing authors are based in Norway.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It is recorded in 2 library collections. The work was funded by European Research Council.</p>",
